<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/roof-missing.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/roof-missing-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/roof-missing.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="854" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-guides/">Guides</a></li><li>Hail Damage Documentation for Northwest Arkansas Roofs</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker kicker-l">Guide · 6 min read · June 9, 2026</p><h1>Hail Damage Documentation for Northwest Arkansas Roofs</h1><p class="lede">Benton and Washington counties see more hail than most of the state. Good documentation decides how those roof claims end.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap two"><article class="prose">
<p>Northwest Arkansas roofs take a beating. With repeated spring hailstorms across Benton and Washington counties, many homes have had more than one roof claim, and carriers look closely at storm dates and prior damage.</p>
<h2>Establish the storm date</h2>
<p>Note the date and time of the storm and save any weather alerts you received. Hail reports from the National Weather Service and hail-mapping services can support the date. Photos of hail on the ground, with something for scale, are valuable.</p>
<h2>Document collateral damage</h2>
<p>Before anyone climbs the roof, photograph dents on gutters, downspouts, mailboxes, AC fins, window wraps and painted surfaces. These marks help show the storm’s size and direction.</p>
<h2>Test squares on every slope</h2>
<p>A roofer or appraiser marks a 10-by-10-foot square on each slope and counts and photographs the hits. Hail damage varies by direction, so slopes facing the storm usually show more.</p>
<h2>Photos that work</h2>
<ul>
<li>Wide shots showing each slope, then close-ups of individual hits with a chalk circle and a scale.</li>
<li>Close-ups that show fractured mats or exposed fiberglass, not just missing granules.</li>
<li>Photos of the shingle brand and model if visible, and any discontinued-product evidence.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Prior repairs and old damage</h2>
<p>If your roof was repaired or replaced after an earlier storm, keep those invoices. They help separate new damage from old and establish the roof’s age for depreciation.</p>
<p>Use our <a href="/property-claim-tools/roof-pitch-squares-calculator/">roof pitch and squares calculator</a> to check that the estimate’s quantities match your roof.</p><p class="fineprint">General information, not legal advice. Policy wording and Arkansas law control.</p><h2>Keep reading</h2><div class="rel3"><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/appraisal-guides/river-flood-vs-wind-coverage/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/arkansas-river-valley.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/arkansas-river-valley-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/arkansas-river-valley.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1024" height="712" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="gcard-b"><p class="meta">May 12, 2026 · 6 min read</p><h3><a href="/appraisal-guides/river-flood-vs-wind-coverage/">River Flooding vs. Wind Damage: Where Policies Draw the Line</a></h3><p>After the 2019 Arkansas River flood and every big storm since, the line between flood and wind has shaped thousands of claims.</p></div></article><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/appraisal-guides/arkansas-appraisal-clause-basics/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/meeting.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/meeting-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/meeting.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1024" height="680" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="gcard-b"><p class="meta">Oct 6, 2026 · 7 min read</p><h3><a href="/appraisal-guides/arkansas-appraisal-clause-basics/">How the Appraisal Clause Works in an Arkansas Policy</a></h3><p>A plain-English walk through the appraisal condition found in most Arkansas property policies, and the mistakes that weaken it.</p></div></article><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/appraisal-guides/labor-depreciation-arkansas-acv/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="960" height="640" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="gcard-b"><p class="meta">Sep 22, 2026 · 6 min read</p><h3><a href="/appraisal-guides/labor-depreciation-arkansas-acv/">Labor Depreciation and ACV Payments in Arkansas</a></h3><p>Your first check is usually actual cash value. How depreciation was calculated, including on labor, can change it by thousands.</p></div></article></div></article>
